# CI & SonarCloud Setup Guide — Angular/Nx Microfrontend

## Overview

This guide documents CI and SonarCloud setup for an Angular/Nx workspace using GitHub Actions. It covers the `sonar-scanner` CLI (not the .NET `dotnet-sonarscanner`), lcov coverage format, and Nx-specific patterns.

---

## 1. Workflow Architecture — Two Files

Use **two separate workflow files** to avoid duplicate runs on PRs.

| File | Trigger | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `pr-check.yml` | `pull_request` targeting `main`, `develop` | Build + test + lint + Sonar PR gate |
| `deploy.yml` | `push` to `main`, `develop` | Build + test + Sonar branch tracking |

---

## 2. SonarCloud Free Plan — Hard Limits

| Feature | Free Plan | Paid Plan |
|---|---|---|
| Branch analysis (`sonar.branch.name`) | ❌ NOT supported | ✅ |
| PR analysis | ✅ (PRs targeting default branch only) | ✅ |
| Default branch analysis | ✅ | ✅ |

### Critical rule: never use `sonar.branch.name` on free plan

### Critical rule: only gate PRs targeting `main`

Use `if: github.base_ref == 'main'` on all Sonar steps.

---

## 3. sonar-scanner CLI (Node.js)

For Angular/TypeScript projects, use the **Node.js sonar-scanner** (not the .NET scanner). Install it as a dev dependency or use `npx`:

```bash
npx sonar-scanner \
  -Dsonar.projectKey="your-project-key" \
  -Dsonar.organization="your-org" \
  -Dsonar.host.url="https://sonarcloud.io" \
  -Dsonar.token="${SONAR_TOKEN}" \
  -Dsonar.sources="libs" \
  -Dsonar.tests="libs" \
  -Dsonar.test.inclusions="**/*.spec.ts" \
  -Dsonar.typescript.lcov.reportPaths="coverage/**/lcov.info" \
  -Dsonar.exclusions="node_modules/**,dist/**,.nx/**" \
  -Dsonar.coverage.exclusions="**/*.spec.ts,**/test-setup.ts"
```

Alternatively, create a `sonar-project.properties` file in the workspace root:

```properties
sonar.projectKey=your-project-key
sonar.organization=your-org
sonar.host.url=https://sonarcloud.io
sonar.sources=libs
sonar.tests=libs
sonar.test.inclusions=**/*.spec.ts
sonar.typescript.lcov.reportPaths=coverage/**/lcov.info
sonar.exclusions=node_modules/**,dist/**,.nx/**
sonar.coverage.exclusions=**/*.spec.ts,**/test-setup.ts
```

---

## 4. Coverage Reporting with Nx + Jest

Generate lcov coverage reports using Nx:

```bash
nx test {{ model.manifest.service_name }} --coverage --coverageReporters=lcov
```

Or for all projects:

```bash
nx run-many --target=test --all --coverage --coverageReporters=lcov
```

This produces `coverage/libs/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}/lcov.info`.

### Jest config (jest.config.ts)

Ensure your Jest config includes:

```typescript
export default {
  coverageDirectory: '../../coverage/libs/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}',
  coverageReporters: ['lcov', 'text-summary'],
};
```

---

## 5. PR Analysis Parameters

For `pr-check.yml`, pass PR params:

```bash
-Dsonar.pullrequest.key="${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}" \
-Dsonar.pullrequest.branch="${{ github.head_ref }}" \
-Dsonar.pullrequest.base="${{ github.base_ref }}"
```

---

## 6. The Bootstrap Problem — First Merge to Main

1. Temporarily set `sonar.qualitygate.wait=false` in `pr-check.yml`
2. Merge the first PR to `main` — this seeds the SonarCloud baseline
3. Open a follow-up PR that flips back to `sonar.qualitygate.wait=true`

---

## 7. Quality Gate Strategy

| Workflow | `qualitygate.wait` | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| `deploy.yml` (push to main) | `false` | Tracks health, never blocks CI |
| `pr-check.yml` (PR to main) | `true` | Enforces quality on new code |

The 80% coverage condition applies to **new code lines in the PR only**.

---

## 8. Complete Reference — pr-check.yml

```yaml
name: PR Check

on:
  pull_request:
    branches: [main, develop]

jobs:
  build-test-scan:
    name: Build · Test · Lint · SonarQube
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v5
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0

      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'
          cache: 'npm'

      - run: npm ci

      - name: Lint
        run: nx lint {{ model.manifest.service_name }}

      - name: Test with coverage
        run: nx test {{ model.manifest.service_name }} --coverage --coverageReporters=lcov

      - name: Build
        run: nx build {{ model.manifest.service_name }} --configuration=production

      - name: SonarCloud Scan
        if: github.base_ref == 'main'
        env:
          SONAR_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SONAR_TOKEN }}
        run: |
          npx sonar-scanner \
            -Dsonar.projectKey="your-project-key" \
            -Dsonar.organization="your-org" \
            -Dsonar.host.url="https://sonarcloud.io" \
            -Dsonar.token="${SONAR_TOKEN}" \
            -Dsonar.sources="libs" \
            -Dsonar.tests="libs" \
            -Dsonar.test.inclusions="**/*.spec.ts" \
            -Dsonar.typescript.lcov.reportPaths="coverage/**/lcov.info" \
            -Dsonar.exclusions="node_modules/**,dist/**,.nx/**" \
            -Dsonar.coverage.exclusions="**/*.spec.ts,**/test-setup.ts" \
            -Dsonar.pullrequest.key="${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}" \
            -Dsonar.pullrequest.branch="${{ github.head_ref }}" \
            -Dsonar.pullrequest.base="${{ github.base_ref }}" \
            -Dsonar.qualitygate.wait=true
```

---

## 9. Complete Reference — deploy.yml

```yaml
name: Deploy

on:
  push:
    branches: [main, develop]
  workflow_dispatch:

jobs:
  build-test-scan:
    name: Build · Test · SonarQube
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v5
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0

      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'
          cache: 'npm'

      - run: npm ci

      - name: Test with coverage
        run: nx test {{ model.manifest.service_name }} --coverage --coverageReporters=lcov

      - name: Build
        run: nx build {{ model.manifest.service_name }} --configuration=production

      - name: SonarCloud Scan
        if: github.ref_name == 'main' || github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'
        env:
          SONAR_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SONAR_TOKEN }}
        run: |
          npx sonar-scanner \
            -Dsonar.projectKey="your-project-key" \
            -Dsonar.organization="your-org" \
            -Dsonar.host.url="https://sonarcloud.io" \
            -Dsonar.token="${SONAR_TOKEN}" \
            -Dsonar.sources="libs" \
            -Dsonar.tests="libs" \
            -Dsonar.test.inclusions="**/*.spec.ts" \
            -Dsonar.typescript.lcov.reportPaths="coverage/**/lcov.info" \
            -Dsonar.exclusions="node_modules/**,dist/**,.nx/**" \
            -Dsonar.coverage.exclusions="**/*.spec.ts,**/test-setup.ts" \
            -Dsonar.qualitygate.wait=false
```

---

## 10. Setup Checklist for a New Repo

```
[ ] Create SonarCloud project — note the project key and org slug
[ ] Add SONAR_TOKEN as a GitHub Actions secret
[ ] Remove repo from SonarCloud GitHub App scope (prevents triple runs)
[ ] Add pr-check.yml and deploy.yml using the templates above
[ ] Push to develop — Deploy runs build+test only (no Sonar on develop, free plan)
[ ] Open develop → main PR — PR Check runs Sonar with wait=false (bootstrap)
[ ] Merge the PR — Deploy on main seeds the SonarCloud baseline
[ ] In SonarCloud UI: rename master → main (Administration → Branches)
[ ] Open follow-up PR: flip pr-check.yml back to qualitygate.wait=true
[ ] Done — all future PRs to main are quality gated on new code
```
